  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed first-floor wraparound extension, hip-to-gable roof extension and rear dormer would, by reason of their cumulative scale, bulk and design, result in an incongruous and top-heavy form of development. The extensions would appear conspicuous and out of keeping with the prevailing scale, form and character of surrounding dwellings, causing material harm to the character and appearance of the host property and the wider streetscene. Furthermore, the proposed use as a large HMO accommodating up to eight occupants would result in a significant intensification of activity compared with a single-family dwelling. The associated comings and goings of occupants, visitors and vehicles would generate increased noise and disturbance, further eroding the established residential character of this densely built-up area. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies D3 and D4 of the London Plan (2021), Core Policies CP5 and CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), Policies DMD5, DMD8, DMD13, DMD14 and DMD37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), and the National Planning Policy Framework (2026).",
    "The applicant has failed to demonstrate, through the submission of a robust parking stress survey and supporting evidence, that the parking demand arising from the proposed 8-bedroom, 8-person House in Multiple Occupation (HMO) can be accommodated within the surrounding highway network without resulting in unacceptable parking stress, displacement parking, or harm to highway safety and the efficient operation of the local road network. In the absence of sufficient evidence to demonstrate that the transport impacts of the development would be acceptable, the Local Planning Authority is unable to conclude that the proposal would not result in adverse impacts on the surrounding highway network. The proposal is therefore contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2026), Policies T4 (Assessing and Mitigating Transport Impacts) and T6.1 (Residential Parking) of the London Plan (2021), Core Policy CP24 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), and Policies DMD 5 and DMD45 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The submission fails to demonstrate that the proposed development, particularly the ground-floor bedrooms, would be safe from surface water and fluvial flooding over its lifetime, taking account of climate change, and, would not increasing flood risk elsewhere.  As such, the proposal has failed to demonstrate that the development would provide safe and satisfactory accommodation for future occupiers or incorporate sufficient flood resistance, resilience and practical mitigation measure. The proposal is therefore contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2026), Policies SI12 and SI13 of the London Plan (2021), Core Policy CP28 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), and Policies DMD59 and DMD61 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).\r"
  ],
